  "subtitle": "Main flow: atomic rolling rate-limit decision → safe redirect → independent click logging.",
  "classNote": "Defaults: 10 accepted clicks/second and 60/minute per IP hash across links. Redis Lua windows and local RAM fallback are caches, not Prisma tables; monitoring is documented separately.",
  "notes": [
    "Lua atomically prunes, counts and inserts allowed requests; denied requests are not inserted. Rolling windows are 1s/60s; key cleanup TTLs are 3s/70s. These are different durations.",
    "Redis failure/timeout uses per-process RAM and sets isDegraded=true; it is not a shared multi-instance limiter. Caller timeout defaults to 50ms. Denial suppresses new attribution, not safe product navigation.",
    "Regular browser and safe available link shown. Worker may run before or after redirect. New invalid logs increment totalClicks, never uniqueClicks; eventId prevents repeated writes. Full details: FR14_CODE_ANALYSIS.md."
  ],
